==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Corruption of "three needle", from the arms of the Needle-makers' Company. Influenced by [[thread]]ing a [[needle]].

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=Threadneedle [[street|Street]]}}

# A [[street]] in [[London]], running from [[Poultry]] and [[Lombard Street]] to [[Bishopsgate]]; the site of the {{w|Bank of England}}.
# {{lb|en|British|economics|banking|finance}} The {{w|Bank of England}}.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=March 6 2008|title=Eddie George defends role of FSA in Northern Rock crisis|journal=w:The Guardian
|passage=George, known as Steady Eddie during his 10 years in charge at '''Threadneedle Street''', said critics who attacked the Financial Services Authority were also wide of the mark.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 11 2007|title=Gieve’s head will not be enough to appease critics|author=Patrick Hosking|journal=w:The Times
|passage=Monetary policy may not be perfect, but it has been far better handled since the responsibility for it moved from 11 Downing Street to '''Threadneedle Street'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=November 10 2002|title=Doing the Continental|author=Faisal Islam|journal=w:The Observer
|passage=The Bank of England cut 0.25 per cent at each meeting - the same decision, spread over two months. Strip out that and Frankfurt and '''Threadneedle Street''' have been running the same policy for a year and a half.}}

